<onlyinclude>The '''noosphere''' is a historical philosophical and scientific concept referring to the sphere or planetary influence of human thought, knowledge and activity. Its early development involved Vladimir Vernadsky, Édouard Le Roy and Pierre Teilhard de Chardin.

== Explanation ==
Vernadsky emphasized human scientific activity as a force transforming the biosphere. Teilhard developed a broader evolutionary and spiritual account of collective thought. Their ideas overlap historically but differ in assumptions. Human alteration of Earth is observable; a planetary mind or predetermined spiritual destination is not thereby established.

